# Brother b-PAC SDK vendor file — COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, do not re-add this rule.
#
# `public/vendor/bpac.js` is Brother's, and it arrives with the b-PAC SDK installer
# rather than from npm. It used to be ignored, on the grounds that Brother's licence
# does not permit redistribution — and that was right, and it was also the reason
# **silent printing worked on localhost and not on the deployed site.**
#
# A gitignored file is not in the deployment, and `vercel.json`'s SPA rewrite answers
# any path missing from the filesystem with `index.html` — *successfully*. Measured:
#
#   GET /vendor/bpac.js  ->  200, text/html, 495 bytes, body "<!DOCTYPE html>…"
#
# The loader fetched that 200, wrapped it in a blob, and `import()` handed the module
# parser an HTML document, which surfaced to the operator as
# `SyntaxError: Unexpected token '<'` — a message naming neither the cause nor the fix.
#
# The file is therefore tracked. Refresh it from
# `C:\Program Files (x86)\Brother bPAC3 SDK\Samples\JavaScript\bpac.js`.
# See src/modules/assets/services/bpacService.ts.
